feat(user-tokens): contact detail and timeline for token desktop sessions

Why: the user answered "Yes, on by default" for contact timelines in a
desktop session started from a user token; clicking a person in the CRM
needs the contact record and its timeline, both refused to a bound session.
What: waiver W4 on the bound delegated door only, exact keys for contact
detail and contact timeline, ability crm + read, no org opt-in and no
session-actions switch. The org CRM switch and a new org opt-out
(userTokens.contactTimelines false) apply to both routes. Operator tokens
get no W4. Bearer answers are unchanged in every switch state; snapshot and
subset pins carry a carve-out naming exactly the two keys.
Testing: from apps/api on t2-dev, vitest run of the new
user-token-contact-timeline-default test (red first: 9 of 12 failed on
72290cc761e), the inventory, delegation, bearer-parity, rt3, desktop-session
and gmail-limited-use suites green (user-tokens-policy keeps its 2 baseline
failures), tsc clean, 4 mutants killed.
Refs: GoodQA #15561

